# Update sitemap on public page changes (Negative Space Works)

When public site URLs change on this GitHub Pages site, update `sitemap.xml` in the **same change** (or same PR). Do not leave sitemap updates for a follow-up.

## Must update

Update `sitemap.xml` when you:

1. Add a public page
2. Remove a public page
3. Rename a page or change its path
4. Add a locale alternate that needs `hreflang` in the sitemap

## Usually skip

Skip a required sitemap edit when the change is **copy- or design-only** on an existing URL. An optional `lastmod` bump is fine; it is not required.

## Origin and robots

- Use the real origin `https://negativespace.works` (check `CNAME`; do not invent hosts).
- Keep `robots.txt`’s `Sitemap:` pointer correct if the sitemap path ever moves.

## Structure

Preserve the existing sitemap structure: URL list plus `xhtml:link` hreflang alternates (`en`, `ja`, `x-default`) as already present. Match the pattern of neighboring `<url>` entries when adding or editing entries.

## Related

For new page meta/copy, follow `.cursor/rules/english-first-copy.mdc` (English first; Japanese is a translation).
